# Security headers for choirulhaq.com (Cloudflare Pages).
#
# Rules learned here the hard way — the grade on this site went A+ to D when a
# single block failed to parse, so keep the shape of this file stable:
#
#   1. One block per URL pattern. This file uses exactly ONE `/*` block.
#      Two blocks matching `/*` merged unpredictably and the security headers
#      in the first one were silently dropped (observed live: HTML served only
#      x-content-type-options + referrer-policy, no CSP/HSTS/X-Frame-Options).
#   2. NO comment lines inside a header block. Comments live between blocks,
#      at column 0, as the Cloudflare docs example shows them. A `#` line
#      indented inside a block is what preceded the D-grade incident.
#   3. Cache-Control belongs in this same block, not in a second `/*` block.
#
# CSP notes: the floating anchor ad loads Google AdSense, which needs its own
# origins. Without these the ad slot renders empty and the console reports a
# CSP violation — ads silently fail rather than render.
#   script-src : pagead2 (loader) + tpc.googlesyndicate (ad delivery) +
#                partner.googleadservices + googletagservices (creatives).
#   img-src    : ad images and tracking pixels are not same-origin.
#   frame-src  : some ad formats render inside an iframe, so this must list
#                the ad hosts rather than being omitted.
#   connect-src: ad measurement / verification calls.
# frame-ancestors stays 'none' — that direction controls who may frame THIS
# page, which is unrelated to the ad's own child iframe (frame-src).
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com https://tpc.googlesyndication.com https://partner.googleadservices.com https://www.googletagservices.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://ui-avatars.com https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com https://tpc.googlesyndication.com https://www.google.com https://googleusercontent.com; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com https://tpc.googlesyndication.com; frame-src https://googleads.g.doubleclick.net https://tpc.googlesyndication.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; form-action 'self'
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

# Astro fingerprints the filenames it builds into /_astro/, so those URLs
# change whenever the content does and can be cached forever. That is the
# safe place for `immutable`.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Content-hashed by name — same reasoning as above.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

# Files served from a STABLE path must be revalidated rather than cached for a
# year. `immutable` on a stable path means an edit stays invisible to every
# visitor who already loaded it (observed: age 4270s against a 31536000s
# max-age, cf-cache-status HIT), and a reload cannot fix that. A max-age of
# 3600 keeps the fast path — the edge still answers 304 — while guaranteeing a
# fresh copy is eventually seen.
/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
